---
title: "Provided Cell Editors"
---

The grid provides several built-in cell editors for common data types.

-   [Text Cell Editor](./provided-cell-editors-text/) — default editor for string columns; uses the standard HTML text `input`.
-   [Large Text Cell Editor](./provided-cell-editors-large-text/) — multi-line textarea editor displayed as a popup; use for longer string values.
-   [Select Cell Editor](./provided-cell-editors-select/) — basic HTML `<select>` drop-down; simple to configure but has browser limitations (see that page for details). Prefer the Rich Select editor for richer keyboard and UX behaviour.
-   [Rich Select Cell Editor](./provided-cell-editors-rich-select/) {% enterpriseIcon /%} — virtualised drop-down with search, filtering, multi-selection, and custom cell renderer support; recommended over the Select editor for most use cases.
-   [Formula Cell Editor](./formula-editor-component/) {% enterpriseIcon /%} — spreadsheet-style formula input for cells backed by formula data.

The following editors are primarily designed for use with [Cell Data Types](./cell-data-types/), which configures them automatically for the corresponding column type:

-   [Number Cell Editor](./provided-cell-editors-number/) — numeric `input` with configurable `min`, `max`, step, and precision; supports keyboard increment/decrement via {% kbd "↑" /%} {% kbd "↓" /%}.
-   [Date Cell Editor](./provided-cell-editors-date/) — standard HTML date `input`; two variants for `Date` objects (`agDateCellEditor`) and ISO date strings (`agDateStringCellEditor`).
-   [Checkbox Cell Editor](./provided-cell-editors-checkbox/) — boolean toggle; normally paired with the Checkbox Cell Renderer so the checkbox is always visible in the cell.

